# ==============================================================================
# NutriFridge — n8n Cloud Configuration Guide
# ==============================================================================
# NOTE: When running on n8n Cloud (https://app.n8n.cloud/), server-level .env 
# variables ($env.VAR) are NOT used for credentials. 
#
# Instead, n8n Cloud uses its built-in Credentials manager.
# You must create TWO Header Auth credentials in the n8n Cloud web interface:
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Webhook Authentication Credential
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Type: Header Auth (httpHeaderAuth)
# Credential Name: NutriFridge Webhook Secret
# Header Name: x-webhook-secret
# Header Value: <YOUR_SECURE_SHARED_SECRET>
#
# * Note: This secret must match the N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET configured in your
#   Supabase Edge Function environment secrets.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Google Gemini API Credential
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Type: Header Auth (httpHeaderAuth)
# Credential Name: Google Gemini API Key
# Header Name: x-goog-api-key
# Header Value: <YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY_FROM_GOOGLE_AI_STUDIO>
#
# * Note: Obtain an API key from Google AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com/).
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Model Configuration
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The workflow is preconfigured with the stable Gemini 3.8 Flash model:
# https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/gemini-3.8-flash:generateContent
# No environment variable or server configuration is required.
# ==============================================================================
